        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(shared): add unit tests for levenshteinDistance",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Problem: `levenshteinDistance` is an exported pure function used for fuzzy string matching but has 0% test coverage.\n- Root cause: No test file existed.\n- Fix: Add 11 unit tests covering identical strings, empty inputs, single-char differences, classic edit distance, insertion/deletion, case sensitivity, Unicode, and longer strings.\n- Out of scope: No source changes; test-only addition.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: `levenshteinDistance` computes edit distance between two strings.\n- Real environment tested: Node.js v22, production `levenshteinDistance` from `src/shared/levenshtein-distance.js`\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch: imported the production module via `node --import tsx -e`\n- Evidence after fix:\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx -e \"import { levenshteinDistance } from ./src/shared/levenshtein-distance.js\"\n\nlevenshteinDistance(\"kitten\", \"sitting\") = 3\nlevenshteinDistance(\"\", \"abc\") = 3\nlevenshteinDistance(\"abc\", \"\") = 3\nlevenshteinDistance(\"cat\", \"cats\") = 1\nlevenshteinDistance(\"hello\", \"hello\") = 0\n\n$ npx vitest run src/shared/levenshtein-distance.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  11 passed (11)\n```\n\n- Observed result after fix: All 11 tests pass matching expected edit distances.\n- What was not tested: Performance on strings >1000 characters.",
